From: Chokri Hammedi <52697989+blue0x1@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] debug: log what GPU memory is live, grouped by kind

With the GPU memory log on, every image and buffer allocation is tracked
until it is freed. Every 256 submits, and when a submit fails, the log lists
the live total for images and for buffers and the 25 largest groups (images
by size and format, buffers by usage). Not for a release.

diff --git a/src/graphics/host_gpu/graphicContext.h b/src/graphics/host_gpu/graphicContext.h
index 09233a7d6c9cc48ffe26a9526d814dfcf8e2dabc..5022db76253c511238417a2a55d9ee5d34fb8453 100644
--- a/src/graphics/host_gpu/graphicContext.h
+++ b/src/graphics/host_gpu/graphicContext.h
@@ -114,6 +114,9 @@ struct GraphicContext {
 	// KYTY_GPU_MEM_LOG (or a gpu-mem-log file in the working folder): log GPU memory use.
 	[[nodiscard]] static bool GpuMemoryLogEnabled();
 	void NoteAllocation(const char* kind, VmaAllocation allocation, const std::string& what) const;
+	static void NoteFree(VmaAllocation allocation);
+	// What is allocated right now, by kind and size, largest first.
+	static std::string LiveMemorySummary();
 	[[nodiscard]] bool CanReportMemoryUsage() const noexcept { return memory_budget_ext_enabled; }
 	[[nodiscard]] uint64_t GetDeviceMemoryUsage() const;
 	[[nodiscard]] uint64_t GetTotalMemoryBudget() const;
diff --git a/src/graphics/host_gpu/renderer/cache/streamBuffer.cpp b/src/graphics/host_gpu/renderer/cache/streamBuffer.cpp
index 2d8261e469b06340914b6e5ed1aadf4fe97ad67f..d2da9fa5c461b0cac5fcbd82183eaf158e82fc12 100644
